    "props": {
      "also_text": "Arcane Duelist, Magic Knight, Blade Mage",
      "benefit_dropdown": "choice_benefit",
      "classMechanic_text": "<h1>Resonance</h1><p></p><h2>SYMPHONY OF MAGIC AND STEEL</h2><p><strong>Resonance</strong> represents the harmony between your blade and spellcraft—an energy that builds as you weave martial strikes with arcane precision. As your control over both disciplines grows, so too does your ability to blend them into a seamless rhythm of offense.</p><p></p><h2>GAINING RESONANCE</h2><p>You begin generating Resonance once you acquire the <strong>【Spellweave】</strong> skill. Each time you cast an <strong>Offensive Spell</strong> and follow up with an <strong>【Attack】</strong> action (excluding Free Attacks), you gain 1 Resonance at the end of your turn.</p><p>The maximum amount of Resonance you can store is equal to your <strong>【Spellweave】</strong> level +1. All Resonance is lost when the scene ends.</p><p></p><h2>SPENDING RESONANCE</h2><p>Resonance can be expended in various ways, such as enhancing spell potency through <strong>【Spellweave】</strong>—increasing your <strong>Magic Check</strong> by 1 for each point spent—or unlocking advanced techniques like <strong>【Spellblade Rhapsody】</strong>, which allows you to cast an <strong>Offensive Spell</strong> and strike in the same turn.</p><p>Other skills, like <strong>【Bladework】</strong>, synergize with your spellcasting by refunding MP if you attacked after casting. This creates a tempo-based playstyle where alternating between spells and attacks keeps your momentum flowing.</p><p>Mastering Resonance means playing both parts of the symphony—ensuring neither blade nor spell stands alone.</p>",
